        <p>Northern Union. Annual Report and Balance Sheet.</p>
        <p>The report and balance-sheet of the Northern Union was presented at the annual general meeting on Friday and furnishes interesting reading, The Union still maintains its strengto and power, and proof of this fact is furnished in the balance-sheet, which shows the Union as holding a substantial balance in hand of £2,334 19s 9.1. During the forthcoming season the Northern Union will extend its boundaries to the county of Durham. the South Shields Clubs having been ad- mitted to membership. The honours of County Cham- pionship were again aecurei by Lancashire last seasen, while Batley were credited with the Northern Union Cup. The committee regret they have to report that they are about to lose the services of Messrs C A Brewer and A Fattorini.</p>
        <p>Meeting at Huddersfield.</p>
        <p>On Tuesday night,a—meeting was held at Huddersfield of Northern League Clubs and Yorkshire Second Com- petition Clubs not included in the League. The meeting specially considered the present position of Yorkshire football. Northern League Clubs pointed out that the proposed boycott by the Yorkshire Senior Competition was neither in the interests of the Competition nor of Yorkshire football generally, and the League Committee suggested that the Second Competition clubs who are likely to be taken into the Yorkshire Senior Com- petition to fill up the places of those clubs which have gone into the League, should not support that action. It is understood that Yorkshire Second Com- petition clubs also took that view, and promised to support the action of the Senior Competition in that respect,and use their efforts to avoid friction that at present exists, Efforts were also put forward to make up the fixture lists, but in conseqence of certain clubs not being favourably drawn the result was a deadlock and a sub-committee was appointed to deal with the matter at an early date.</p>
        <p>The Failure of Local Newspaper Proprietors, Theatoublic examination into the affairs of William Skilling residing at the Avenue, Statham, Lymm ; ' and John Shaw Green residing at Urban-road, Sale, carrying on business in co-partnership as news- paper proprietors and publishers under the style of Skilling and Green at 12, Brazennose-street, Man- chester, again came on at the Manchester Bank- ruptcy Court on Monday, betore Mr Registrar Atkinson. The case had been adjourned from May 20th for further accounts. The Official Raceme? (Mr C J Dibb) stated that Mr Skilling had not yet tiled the accounts. They would remember that on the last occasion be mentioned that Mr Green had handed to him a document concerning a third party, He had only that morning received a written reply to :that statement from the third party, and he had bad a similar reply from Mr. Skilling also. He thought the better plan would be to hand these to Mr Skilling. He asked that the matter might be adjourned to September 2nd, so that the accounts could be lodged with him (the Official Receiver.) This was agreed to</p>
