      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-07-12_WidnesExaminer_art0058" n="art0058">
        <head>SUMIIER MONTHS</head>
        <p>SUMIIER MONTHS</p>
        <p>If you ilnd that your system is unable to bear the oppressive heat, and you are almost unable to follow your vocation, immediately strengthen your constitu- tion by taking a course of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. This preparation makes the weak strong, and gives new heart and " go" to the weary toiler. It revives the spirits and strengthens the nerves, and by giving tone to the whole constitution, wards eff fevers, and many other ailments prevalent at this time of the year. No family should be without a bottle in the houtr. An occasional dose, taken when feeling slightly out of sorts, has prevented many a long illness. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is The Best Remedy of The Age for Weakness, Nervousness, Indigestion, LOW Spirits, Sleeplessness, Influenza, and Chest Affections. It is often asked, " How is it that one single medicine like Gwilvm Evans' Quinine Bitters is capable of curing so many different direases ?" The reply,however,is simple enough. Most diseases have. a common source, either in a deranged stomach and its connections, or in weak and impure blood. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, by striking at the root of the evil, by strengthening the stomach and pnrifyinpr the liod, places these impor- tant life sources in proper working order, and the disease, under whatever form it may have shown itself, disappears: Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is sold by all chemists and stores, in bottles 21. 91. and 43.61. each. Refuse to take substitutes. OUR FOOD.</p>
        <p>Constant overworking of the stomach must produce disease of that organ. More nutriment is furnished to the bcdy by a small quantity of food well digested than by a large quantity half digested. The only trustwolthy and permanent remedy is Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, which, acting upon the digestive organs, strethens them and Rtimulates them to healthy action and gives tone to the whole stomach, imparting new life,lf6pfe, strength, and happiness. Overwork ought to be overpaid. Nature insists upon payment of her dues. Inenaie devotion to business gives the digestive organs only a bare chance to perform their work. He who comes in a hurry from active work, rapidly swallows bis food and hurries cut again, is piling up a debt wh'cb Nature makes him pay in a painful dyspeptic experience. Grwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters will help you to pay, anajooner you rake it the better. Delicate patients often Complain that they are unable to take quinine, as it produces headaches, So., but it has been established beyond doubt that Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters has oveiTome this difficulty, containing, as it does other medicinal herbs of great therapeutic value,such as sarsa- parilla, saffron, dandelion, gentian, and lavender, scien- tifically prepared in happy proportions. Gwilym Evan? Quinine Bitters is sold in bottles 25. 91. and 4s. 131. eaell; by all chemists and stores. Beware of imitations. The name " Gwilym vans". 9 must be found on the label, scamn, and bottle, to insure its being genuine. When you Ind the nsme, then you are sure there is no mistake. The Sole Proprietors are The Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, Llanelly, South Wales.</p>
